#: ../../../SanitizerStats.md:1
msgid "SanitizerStats"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SanitizerStats.md:7
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SanitizerStats.md:9
msgid ""
"The sanitizers support a simple mechanism for gathering profiling statistics "
"to help understand the overhead associated with sanitizers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SanitizerStats.md:12
msgid "How to build and run"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SanitizerStats.md:14
msgid ""
"SanitizerStats can currently only be used with {doc}`ControlFlowIntegrity`. "
"In addition to `-fsanitize=cfi*`, pass the `-fsanitize-stats` flag. This "
"will cause the program to count the number of times that each control flow "
"integrity check in the program fires."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SanitizerStats.md:19
msgid ""
"At run time, set the `SANITIZER_STATS_PATH` environment variable to direct "
"statistics output to a file. The file will be written on process exit. The "
"following substitutions will be applied to the environment variable:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SanitizerStats.md:23
msgid "`%b` -- The executable basename."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SanitizerStats.md:24
msgid "`%p` -- The process ID."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SanitizerStats.md:26
msgid ""
"You can also send the `SIGUSR2` signal to a process to make it write "
"sanitizer statistics immediately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SanitizerStats.md:29
msgid ""
"The `sanstats` program can be used to dump statistics. It takes as a command "
"line argument the path to a statistics file produced by a program compiled "
"with `-fsanitize-stats`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SanitizerStats.md:33
msgid ""
"The output of `sanstats` is in four columns, separated by spaces. The first "
"column is the file and line number of the call site. The second column is "
"the function name. The third column is the type of statistic gathered (in "
"this case, the type of control flow integrity check). The fourth column is "
"the call count."
msgstr ""

